# 6. CALIPER — PROJECT ENGINEERING CONSTITUTION

CALIPER is one of the most important components of H-Caliper.

Every project must have its own CALIPER directory.

CALIPER contains the engineering principles that govern how the AI agents must understand, plan, implement, test, and modify the project.

The factory must load relevant CALIPER principles before every production task.

Create the following 12 mandatory principle documents:

1. test.md
   Test Principles

2. logs.md
   Logging Principles

3. graph.md
   Graph and System Modeling Principles

4. security.md
   Security Principles

5. business.md
   Business Principles

6. architecture.md
   Clean Architecture and Design Pattern Principles

7. ui-ux.md
   UI/UX Principles

8. git-branches.md
   Git Branching Principles

9. decisions.md
   Technical and Architectural Decisions

10. tech-stack.md
    Technology Stack Principles

11. clean-code.md
    Clean Code Principles

12. performance.md
    Performance Principles

The original project specification refers to 13 CALIPER files but explicitly identifies only 12 principles.

Therefore:

- Implement the 12 defined principle documents.
- Reserve a configurable thirteenth principle slot.
- Do not invent the missing principle.
- Allow an administrator to define and activate it later.

## CALIPER Document Structure

Every principle document should support:

- Purpose.
- Scope.
- Mandatory Rules.
- Recommended Practices.
- Forbidden Practices.
- Validation Criteria.
- Exceptions.
- Approval Requirements.
- Version History.

## CALIPER Governance

Implement version control for CALIPER.

Every change must have:

- Previous version.
- Proposed version.
- Change description.
- Reason for change.
- Related task.
- Author or responsible agent.
- Approval status.
- Timestamp.

AI agents may propose modifications.

They must not silently change mandatory principles.

Require explicit approval for changes to protected principles.

