# 8. PRODUCTION PIPELINE ORCHESTRATION

Implement a persistent workflow engine.

The pipeline must follow this sequence:

USER REQUEST
    |
    v
TASK CREATION
    |
    v
WORKSPACE CONTEXT COLLECTION
    |
    v
CALIPER PRINCIPLE LOADING
    |
    v
PLANNING AGENT
    |
    v
PLAN VALIDATION
    |
    v
EXECUTION AGENT
    |
    v
AUTOMATED QUALITY GATES
    |
    v
REVIEW AGENT
    |
    +----------------------+
    |                      |
    v                      v
  ACCEPTED               REJECTED
    |                      |
    v                      v
DOCUMENTATION          RETURN TO PLANNING
    |                      |
    v                      v
RELEASE PREPARATION    REVISED PLAN
    |
    v
HUMAN APPROVAL
    |
    v
OPTIONAL DEPLOYMENT
    |
    v
TASK COMPLETED

## Rejection and Retry Logic

When the Review Agent rejects a task:

1. Save the review report.
2. Preserve the execution artifacts.
3. Send the rejection report to the Planning Agent.
4. Generate a revised plan.
5. Execute the revised plan.
6. Run validation again.
7. Request another review.

Implement configurable maximum retry limits.

Never create infinite execution loops.

Allow human intervention at any stage.

## Task States

Implement persistent states such as:

- CREATED
- CONTEXT_COLLECTION
- PLANNING
- PLAN_REVIEW
- READY_FOR_EXECUTION
- EXECUTING
- AUTOMATED_VALIDATION
- AI_REVIEW
- REJECTED
- REPLANNING
- DOCUMENTATION
- AWAITING_APPROVAL
- RELEASE_READY
- DEPLOYING
- COMPLETED
- FAILED
- CANCELLED
- BLOCKED

Every state transition must be recorded.

The workflow must survive application restarts.

Do not depend on in-memory state for task persistence.

